# write returns null; verify that the read handle has the expected Readable cap
# % is used as an intermediate expression to force the write side-effect.
# has-cap? is now in stdlib/io.llt — include it in the same doc as the usage
[write-file [narrow %cwd "target"] "tinct-test-write-caps.txt" "caps check"]
---
%
[include %libdir "io.llt"]
[has-cap? [open [narrow %cwd "target"] "tinct-test-write-caps.txt" Readable] "Readable"]


=== out
Bool(true)

=== warn
[UndefinedVariable] undefined variable: has-cap?
